{
  "_comment": "Engine packages: everything that is specific to one platform (GPU runtime libraries and the CLI builds the pipelines run), installed as a unit under ENGINES_DIR/<id>/<version>/ and loaded by app/engines/. The server itself holds no GPU code, so a package can be installed, switched or reloaded while the server runs. Every download is pinned by URL, size and SHA256 like catalog/models.json. A package's runners name the CLIs the pipelines ask for (sd-cli: stable-diffusion.cpp, trellis-cli: trellis.cpp) with their library directories.  A package may also build a CLI from pinned sources (\"build\", app/engines/build.py) where upstream publishes no binary. Bumping a version means a new package version (all items reviewed together) and a CHANGELOG.md entry.",
  "version": 1,
  "_hosts": "A download (and every redirect it follows) must be https and its host must equal one of these domains or end with '.' + one of them (CDN hosts vary, e.g. us.aws.cdn.hf.co, release-assets.githubusercontent.com).",
